":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}","name":"Sphere of Resistance","oracle_id":"09c96077-3804-4f12-a613-5bebc5e0413f","oracle_text":"Spells cost {1} more to cast.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2014-06-16","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Twiddle","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","oracle_text":"You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2003-07-28","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"It affects all players, including you.","oracle_id":"09c96077-3804-4f12-a613-5bebc5e0413f","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Battlefield Thaumaturge's first ability doesn't change that spell's mana cost or mana value. It changes only the amount you actually pay (the \u201ctotal cost\u201d of the spell).","oracle_id":"70d2f5f7-f727-48e1-9532-8d365b1c1ae5","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Heroic abilities will resolve before the spell that caused them to trigger.","oracle_id":"70d2f5f7-f727-48e1-9532-8d365b1c1ae5","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Heroic abilities will trigger only once per spell, even if that spell targets the creature with the heroic ability multiple times.","oracle_id":"70d2f5f7-f727-48e1-9532-8d365b1c1ae5","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Heroic abilities won't trigger when a copy of a spell is created on the stack or when a spell's targets are changed to include a creature with a heroic ability.","oracle_id":"70d2f5f7-f727-48e1-9532-8d365b1c1ae5","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The cost reduction created by Battlefield Thaumaturge's first ability can reduce only the generic portion of the spell's total cost. Colored mana requirements aren't affected.","oracle_id":"70d2f5f7-f727-48e1-9532-8d365b1c1ae5","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The cost reduction is {1} per target creature, even if the spell targets a creature more than once.","oracle_id":"70d2f5f7-f727-48e1-9532-8d365b1c1ae5","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To calculate the total cost of an instant or sorcery spell you're casting, start with the mana cost (or alternative cost, if applicable), add all cost increases (including additional costs such as those imposed by strive abilities), then subtract all cost reductions (such as the one created by Battlefield Thaumaturge's first ability).","oracle_id":"70d2f5f7-f727-48e1-9532-8d365b1c1ae5","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a spell or ability allows you to cast a strive spell without paying its mana cost, you must pay the additional costs for any targets beyond the first.","oracle_id":"925a0b9b-a1fa-4aad-89d9-e2698ac3582f","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If all of the spell's targets are illegal when the spell tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. If one or more of its targets are legal when it tries to resolve, the spell will resolve and affect only those legal targets. It will have no effect on any illegal targets.","oracle_id":"925a0b9b-a1fa-4aad-89d9-e2698ac3582f","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If such a spell is copied, and the effect that copies the spell allows a player to choose new targets for the copy, the number of targets can't be changed. The player may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, the player can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).","oracle_id":"925a0b9b-a1fa-4aad-89d9-e2698ac3582f","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The mana cost and mana value of strive spells don't change no matter how many targets they have. Strive abilities affect only what you pay.","oracle_id":"925a0b9b-a1fa-4aad-89d9-e2698ac3582f","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose how many targets each spell with a strive ability has and what those targets are as you cast it. It's legal to cast such a spell with no targets, although this is rarely a good idea. You can't choose the same target more than once for a single strive spell.","oracle_id":"925a0b9b-a1fa-4aad-89d9-e2698ac3582f","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Hinata's last two abilities ability count the number of players or objects that are targets of a spell as it is cast, not the number of times the card text uses the word \u201ctarget.\u201d For example, a spell you cast that says \u201ctarget creature\u201d twice would cost {1} less to cast if each instance targeted the same creature and {2} less to cast if they each targeted different creatures.","oracle_id":"aee473c7-c659-421c-96b5-05f57ca2ed97","published_at":"2022-02-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may choose the same creature for both targets. You may also choose two different creatures. This is because the word \u201ctarget\u201d is used twice.","oracle_id":"d52e9255-62e7-479f-8def-e92b96efdb89","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
